WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.500
- Hi, my name's Audrey.

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:02.730
- And I'm Chloe.

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:04.440
- And we're 7 years old

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:06.930
and today two chefs are gonna be competing

00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:10.187
to make our dream outer space dish.

00:00:10.187 --> 00:00:15.187
- [Audrey and Chloe] 3, 2, 1, blast off

00:00:15.675 --> 00:00:17.996
- [Rie and Alix] Hi!

00:00:17.996 --> 00:00:18.829
- I'm Rie.

00:00:18.829 --> 00:00:20.992
- And I'm Alix. I have a question for you.

00:00:20.992 --> 00:00:21.825
- What?

00:00:21.825 --> 00:00:24.660
- If you were going to a
birthday party on Mars,

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:26.370
what food would you wanna eat?

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:30.933
- I would maybe drink a outer space drink.

00:00:30.933 --> 00:00:34.770
It's purple and has little
pieces of stars in it.

00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:36.361
Makes you go a little crazy.

00:00:36.361 --> 00:00:37.560
- Oh!

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:39.270
- I'm drawing a Flower Planet.

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:40.860
- What do you like to eat?

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:42.000
- I like to eat donuts.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.910
- What are the best flavors
on the Flower Planet?

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:46.830
- Strawberry. Lavender.

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:49.530
- Lavender. Do you like
vanilla and chocolate too?

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:52.860
- Yeah, I love chocolate and vanilla,

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:54.420
but she loves chocolate more.

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:56.100
- The picture is very creative

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:59.640
so I'm excited to be creative as well.

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:03.480
- The next thing I'm gonna
draw is the Ice Cream Planet.

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:07.230
Stars taste delicious
since they make wishes.

00:01:07.230 --> 00:01:08.253
- [Rie And Alix] Oh!

00:01:08.253 --> 00:01:11.940
- It's a cookie that
has little stars on it

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:14.100
and it's a big star after stars are on.

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:15.240
- What does it taste like?

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:17.850
- It tastes like a normal cookie

00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:20.340
but in the middle there will be a filling.

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:21.960
- Have you eaten a star before?

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:22.793
- No.

00:01:22.793 --> 00:01:23.626
- No?

00:01:23.626 --> 00:01:24.459
- Yes.

00:01:24.459 --> 00:01:25.292
- Oh, you did?

00:01:25.292 --> 00:01:26.437
- Are you excited for a space party?

00:01:26.437 --> 00:01:27.840
- [Audrey and Chloe] Yeah!

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:30.660
- How about we wish upon
a star and then blast off?

00:01:30.660 --> 00:01:31.618
So...

00:01:31.618 --> 00:01:34.285
- [Everyone] 3, 2, 1. Blast off!

00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:39.900
- Woo! Are you ready?

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:40.980
- I am. Are you?

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:42.720
- I've always wanted to go to space, so...

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:43.830
- I'm not interested.

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:45.513
- Really? They say there's
two kinds of people.

00:01:45.513 --> 00:01:47.790
People who wanna go to deep sea,

00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:49.230
and people who wanna go to deep space.

00:01:49.230 --> 00:01:50.548
- I don't wanna go either.

00:01:50.548 --> 00:01:51.381
(Alix laughs)

00:01:51.381 --> 00:01:53.430
- Gonna take some risks
today, but you know what?

00:01:53.430 --> 00:01:54.300
We're in space.

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:55.242
- Yeah.

00:01:55.242 --> 00:01:56.075
- So...

00:01:56.075 --> 00:01:56.908
- We're gonna just have fun.

00:01:56.908 --> 00:01:57.741
- Always.

00:01:57.741 --> 00:01:58.574
- Aww!

00:01:58.574 --> 00:01:59.407
- I draw your cookies back.

00:01:59.407 --> 00:02:00.510
Yay! Champ is here.

00:02:00.510 --> 00:02:03.750
- As always, I am so excited
to do this show with Rie

00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:05.880
and to get to cook alongside
her like old times.

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:08.280
- I'm going to start with Ice Cream Planet

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:09.810
'cause I need some prep time.

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:11.640
- I'm gonna start with Flower Planet.

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:14.913
Listen, in this competition,
I am not above picnics

00:02:14.913 --> 00:02:16.860
or food coloring as we know.

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:17.693
- Yeah.

00:02:17.693 --> 00:02:18.526
- These are kids.

00:02:18.526 --> 00:02:21.570
- Their taste buds is very sensitive.

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:22.403
- Yes.

00:02:22.403 --> 00:02:24.090
- So they don't like complicated flavor.

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:26.640
- I do wonder if I'm at a disadvantage now

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:28.860
in this competition because Rie is a mom.

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:32.070
- I feel more confident
after I have a child,

00:02:32.070 --> 00:02:33.720
but at the same time,

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:38.490
my son is the pickiest boy in the world.

00:02:38.490 --> 00:02:40.290
- I still think of myself
as a child, though,

00:02:40.290 --> 00:02:42.930
so maybe I can relate to
the judges a little better.

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:47.760
- I'm scooping ice cream
and making a sphere.

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:49.800
- I'm gonna bake my cake on a sheet tray,

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:52.110
just 'cause I want it to bake faster.

00:02:52.110 --> 00:02:54.420
I need a pretty good volume of cakes,

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:55.950
so I'm just gonna make another one

00:02:55.950 --> 00:02:57.600
and put it right back on here.

00:02:57.600 --> 00:02:59.460
- I got a bunch of different fruits

00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:01.740
and I'm gonna start cutting.

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:03.810
- Rie has been making things from scratch

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:05.250
with a lot of natural ingredients.

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:07.050
At first I was a little intimidated,

00:03:07.050 --> 00:03:09.150
but then I remembered
that the judges are kids,

00:03:09.150 --> 00:03:10.770
so I know my audience.

00:03:10.770 --> 00:03:13.590
I'm just gonna try to
make it kind of galaxy-ish

00:03:13.590 --> 00:03:17.370
by just putting a little
black, a little blue.

00:03:17.370 --> 00:03:20.630
Oh! A lot of purple. This looks cool.

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:21.660
- It's like a galaxy.

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:24.960
- Swirly galaxy. Rie, do
you wanna go to space?

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:25.830
- I don't.

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:26.663
- Why?

00:03:26.663 --> 00:03:28.020
- I love ours.

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:31.090
We have to make sure ours
doesn't fall apart and--

00:03:31.090 --> 00:03:31.923
- You're right.

00:03:31.923 --> 00:03:32.756
- We don't need to go.

00:03:32.756 --> 00:03:33.589
- You should stay.

00:03:33.589 --> 00:03:34.620
- What do you do in space?

00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:36.510
- Just chill, you know, vibe.

00:03:36.510 --> 00:03:38.280
- You can chill in a beach.

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:39.974
You have to drink your own urine.

00:03:39.974 --> 00:03:41.040
- No you don't.

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:43.260
- No. I went to NASA and it's--

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:44.476
- Oh, you went to NASA now!

00:03:44.476 --> 00:03:45.309
(Rie laughs)

00:03:45.309 --> 00:03:47.520
I wholeheartedly believe in aliens.

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:50.310
- I don't need to go out to seek aliens.

00:03:50.310 --> 00:03:51.840
They can come to me.

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:52.673
- Yeah.

00:03:52.673 --> 00:03:53.506
- And see me.

00:03:53.506 --> 00:03:54.580
- I was at the Hollywood Bowl last night

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:57.270
and I swear I saw you up front.

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:59.820
- She was explaining what happened,

00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:02.150
but it's just over my head.

00:04:02.150 --> 00:04:04.710
- My swirly galaxy cake is ready to bake.

00:04:04.710 --> 00:04:08.430
- I'm using this pineapple
for the galaxy drink.

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:12.210
- As you can see, I'm back
on another box of cake mix.

00:04:12.210 --> 00:04:14.790
- Alix is using a lot
of store-bought stuff.

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:17.730
I think it is actually a good strategy

00:04:17.730 --> 00:04:21.030
because kids loved sweet stuff.

00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:24.570
- This time I'm going to
add a little bit less liquid

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:26.160
because I'm going to do a hack

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:29.280
where you use cake mix
to make cookie dough.

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:31.200
This is for the star cookie.

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:33.510
- So I'm now cutting mango.

00:04:33.510 --> 00:04:34.950
- I love mango.

00:04:34.950 --> 00:04:35.783
- Do you wanna eat?

00:04:35.783 --> 00:04:36.616
- Yeah.

00:04:36.616 --> 00:04:37.449
- Okay.

00:04:37.449 --> 00:04:38.340
- Remember the good old tasty days--

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:39.173
- Yeah!

00:04:39.173 --> 00:04:40.080
- Where you would feed me all the time?

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:41.970
- We sat next to each other.

00:04:41.970 --> 00:04:43.297
- At first I think you were like,

00:04:43.297 --> 00:04:46.060
"Oh God, who is this girl
sitting next to me? Can I move?"

00:04:46.060 --> 00:04:46.893
(Rie laughs)

00:04:46.893 --> 00:04:48.930
And then at some point
you just accepted it.

00:04:48.930 --> 00:04:50.691
- That's not how I remember, but okay.

00:04:50.691 --> 00:04:51.524
(Alix laughs)

00:04:51.524 --> 00:04:54.900
- I have these neon mixed
sprinkles. They're little stars.

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:57.930
- I remember you are always so fast.

00:04:57.930 --> 00:04:59.250
- I'll be making a lot of mistakes

00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:01.050
and I need the extra time.

00:05:01.050 --> 00:05:04.740
- Once there was a story called
"The Tortoise and the Hare."

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:06.428
- I just try to work fast because I know

00:05:06.428 --> 00:05:08.790
there's gonna be a point
where I mess something up.

00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:11.610
So I wanna leave myself extra
time for that to happen.

00:05:11.610 --> 00:05:14.130
- Now I'm going to make star cookie.

00:05:14.130 --> 00:05:17.010
- I'm gonna be moving on
to my Ice Cream Planets.

00:05:17.010 --> 00:05:21.000
I have these fun Cookie
Crunch Blue Ice Cream

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:23.970
and this one is Mermaid Sparkle Ice Cream.

00:05:23.970 --> 00:05:26.160
I need it patchier, 'cause the Earth,

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:27.960
it's green and blue swirl.

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:32.490
- Oh! I added egg into my butter mixture

00:05:32.490 --> 00:05:34.353
and I'm gonna sift in flour.

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:38.310
- In my mind, this was an amazing idea.

00:05:38.310 --> 00:05:42.321
In reality, it's fine.

00:05:42.321 --> 00:05:43.170
(Rie and Alix laugh)

00:05:43.170 --> 00:05:44.610
- My cookie dough is done,

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:47.040
so I'm going to put this
in the refrigerator.

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:48.179
- Woosh!

00:05:48.179 --> 00:05:49.242
- Woah!

00:05:49.242 --> 00:05:50.075
- My cake is baked.

00:05:50.075 --> 00:05:51.000
- That's so cool!

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:53.790
- I'm just gonna start
tearing this into pieces.

00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:56.700
I really wanna go larger
than life with my dish today.

00:05:56.700 --> 00:06:00.780
So I'm thinking some sort of
giant cake pop as a planet.

00:06:00.780 --> 00:06:02.398
Go to space or go home.

00:06:02.398 --> 00:06:03.231
(Rie laughs)

00:06:03.231 --> 00:06:04.064
- I'd go home.

00:06:04.064 --> 00:06:07.470
I am going to make base of Flower Planet

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:11.401
and I have tofu, I have Mochiko.

00:06:11.401 --> 00:06:12.840
- Oh! Mochi donna?

00:06:12.840 --> 00:06:16.080
- Yeah and squeeze some lemon juice.

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:18.180
- Rie is pulling out tofu.

00:06:18.180 --> 00:06:20.820
If we're supposed to be
providing nutritional value

00:06:20.820 --> 00:06:23.040
to these kids, then I'm going to lose.

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:26.760
- I wanna win, but I also don't
want to give too much sugar.

00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:30.060
- I have this Space Blue Vanilla Frosting.

00:06:30.060 --> 00:06:32.010
Again, I haven't made
a giant cake pop ever

00:06:32.010 --> 00:06:34.170
so this is definitely not going on a stick

00:06:34.170 --> 00:06:35.490
like a normal cake pop would.

00:06:35.490 --> 00:06:39.680
But I'm gonna try to maneuver
some sort of stand for it.

00:06:39.680 --> 00:06:42.123
- So can you still call it cake pop?

00:06:44.130 --> 00:06:47.460
- This is kind of more
difficult than I imagined.

00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:48.630
It kind of breaks apart.

00:06:48.630 --> 00:06:51.388
Because this cake pop is so massive,

00:06:51.388 --> 00:06:54.810
its weight is kind of crushing on itself.

00:06:54.810 --> 00:06:56.807
- How about using plastic wrap?

00:06:56.807 --> 00:06:57.640
(Alix gasps)

00:06:57.640 --> 00:06:58.473
Good idea?

00:06:58.473 --> 00:07:02.730
- But Rie gave me a really
genius tip to use plastic wrap,

00:07:02.730 --> 00:07:05.280
which really helps me
get that sphere shape.

00:07:05.280 --> 00:07:08.910
- I'm just kneading my donut dough

00:07:08.910 --> 00:07:11.400
until everything is smooth.

00:07:11.400 --> 00:07:13.260
I'm going to rest it in the refrigerator

00:07:13.260 --> 00:07:15.870
and I'm going to roll out my cookie dough.

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:17.860
Just cut out star.

00:07:17.860 --> 00:07:19.560
- Can I have some dough?

00:07:19.560 --> 00:07:20.700
- Yeah, are you gonna eat?

00:07:20.700 --> 00:07:21.630
- Do you not like cookie dough?

00:07:21.630 --> 00:07:25.050
- I don't eat cookie dough.
I think it's America thing.

00:07:25.050 --> 00:07:26.040
- You don't eat cookie dough?

00:07:26.040 --> 00:07:26.873
- No.

00:07:26.873 --> 00:07:27.962
- It's so good.

00:07:27.962 --> 00:07:31.290
She has this shooting star
coming out of her drink,

00:07:31.290 --> 00:07:34.530
so I figured it would be
cool to do a sugar one.

00:07:34.530 --> 00:07:36.060
I was just gonna use a Jolly Rancher

00:07:36.060 --> 00:07:40.110
and melt it down so it
would fit in the star.

00:07:40.110 --> 00:07:43.684
We only had a very small
metal star cookie cutter

00:07:43.684 --> 00:07:46.380
so I realized that my Jolly Rancher

00:07:46.380 --> 00:07:47.850
wouldn't quite fit inside it.

00:07:47.850 --> 00:07:50.400
Rie suggested that I smash
it with the rolling pin.

00:07:52.028 --> 00:07:53.160
(Alix gasps, Rie laughs)

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:54.900
Those suckers are hard.

00:07:54.900 --> 00:07:57.120
Who knew that Jolly
Ranchers were so dangerous?

00:07:57.120 --> 00:08:00.433
Okay, I'm gonna put some of
my Jolly Rancher shrapnel

00:08:00.433 --> 00:08:05.190
in here and I just wanted
to melt down into its star.

00:08:05.190 --> 00:08:09.240
- So I'm going to cut out
rice paper in a flower shape.

00:08:09.240 --> 00:08:13.590
This rice paper flower, I saw on TikTok

00:08:13.590 --> 00:08:15.240
and it looked easy enough.

00:08:15.240 --> 00:08:18.270
It's very difficult to cut. It's breaking.

00:08:18.270 --> 00:08:19.500
- Rie is so talented

00:08:19.500 --> 00:08:21.510
and I'm not used to
seeing her make mistakes

00:08:21.510 --> 00:08:25.440
but she's kind of struggling
with the rice paper flowers.

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:26.640
I wish I could help you here

00:08:26.640 --> 00:08:28.200
but I don't know what you're doing.

00:08:28.200 --> 00:08:31.620
I'm gonna use edible flowers
for this reason. Easy enough.

00:08:31.620 --> 00:08:33.750
- How about that? Does
it look like flower?

00:08:33.750 --> 00:08:34.583
- Yeah.

00:08:34.583 --> 00:08:35.416
- Okay.

00:08:35.416 --> 00:08:36.900
- It's like a star
flower, which is perfect.

00:08:36.900 --> 00:08:41.070
- Yeah. From here I think I
can kind of trim into a circle.

00:08:41.070 --> 00:08:44.550
This is becoming a craft, not cooking.

00:08:44.550 --> 00:08:48.060
- Now I'm moving on
finally to my mirror glaze.

00:08:48.060 --> 00:08:50.880
I have my gelatin sheet
and they need to bloom

00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:55.770
I'm gonna add in water, sugar
and sweetened condensed milk.

00:08:55.770 --> 00:08:58.020
And I'm gonna grab my gelatin

00:08:58.020 --> 00:09:01.440
and squeeze out all of the extra water.

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:03.180
Feels like a dead jellyfish.

00:09:03.180 --> 00:09:06.300
Pop this into my sugar
mixture so it can dissolve.

00:09:06.300 --> 00:09:07.785
Now I'm gonna pour my hot mixture

00:09:07.785 --> 00:09:10.740
over this broken-up white chocolate,

00:09:10.740 --> 00:09:12.047
and I want it to be hot enough

00:09:12.047 --> 00:09:14.670
for it to melt the
chocolate along with it.

00:09:14.670 --> 00:09:19.649
Blend up the white
chocolate into my mixture.

00:09:19.649 --> 00:09:21.420
So the galaxy mirror glaze is something

00:09:21.420 --> 00:09:23.580
that's really finicky and hard to do.

00:09:23.580 --> 00:09:25.950
I know that from experience

00:09:25.950 --> 00:09:28.860
but I just want to go for it today.

00:09:28.860 --> 00:09:29.820
I think this might work.

00:09:29.820 --> 00:09:32.160
- I'm gonna make small donuts

00:09:32.160 --> 00:09:34.470
and I'm gonna make two big donuts

00:09:34.470 --> 00:09:36.720
so I have some safety net.

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:39.840
I'm going to make mochi
for my Ice Cream Planet.

00:09:39.840 --> 00:09:42.060
I add Mochiko and sugar

00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:45.540
and I'm lightly mixing, add water, mix.

00:09:45.540 --> 00:09:47.970
Now I'm going to microwave this

00:09:47.970 --> 00:09:50.040
until it becomes sticky and stretchy.

00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:52.170
- So I've separated my mirror glaze

00:09:52.170 --> 00:09:54.150
into five different bowls

00:09:54.150 --> 00:09:56.970
and I'm just gonna be coloring
them different variations

00:09:56.970 --> 00:09:59.760
from black to blue to purple to pink.

00:09:59.760 --> 00:10:02.880
- My cookie is a little softer

00:10:02.880 --> 00:10:06.840
and I'm cutting inside
with another star shape.

00:10:06.840 --> 00:10:10.170
My cookie is out from the oven

00:10:10.170 --> 00:10:13.290
and I'm going to stuff with gummy bear.

00:10:13.290 --> 00:10:17.460
My mochi came out from the
microwave. I'm gonna add color.

00:10:17.460 --> 00:10:21.060
Hope this was a good idea
that's gonna look cute.

00:10:21.060 --> 00:10:24.000
And be very careful when
you're making mochi.

00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:24.833
- Sticky!

00:10:24.833 --> 00:10:27.420
- It's so sticky and it's very, very hot.

00:10:27.420 --> 00:10:31.530
You have to be very
careful. Roll this mochi.

00:10:31.530 --> 00:10:35.790
You have to use a bunch of
corn starch, potato starch.

00:10:35.790 --> 00:10:39.690
You also have to do it
while it's hot. Wow, look!

00:10:39.690 --> 00:10:41.010
- That is beautiful.

00:10:41.010 --> 00:10:42.270
- Yay! Thank you.

